    title: "The Lost Constellation",
    subtitle: "A navigator's quest across uncharted stellar oceans",
    content: `<p>On the edge of the galaxy, the navigator lived in a small, weathered dome that the crew jokingly called his <button class="word-btn" data-word="hut">hut</button>. From this humble starting point, Captain Kael prepared for a journey to the legendary Lost Constellation. The path was uncharted, and the view ahead was <button class="word-btn" data-word="bleak">bleak</button>, filled with cold, empty space. Many in the high command voiced their <button class="word-btn" data-word="disapprobation">disapprobation</button>, calling his mission a dangerous, <button class="word-btn" data-word="fanciful">fanciful</button> waste of resources. But Kael had the <button class="word-btn" data-word="mettle">mettle</button> to withstand their doubts. He possessed a <button class="word-btn" data-word="preternatural">preternatural</button> ability to read star charts, a gift that seemed almost magical.</p><p>As the launch drew near, a <button class="word-btn" data-word="quorum">quorum</button> of officers assembled to review the flight plans. One skeptical captain asked how Kael expected to survive the toxic storms of the outer rim. Kael’s calm <button class="word-btn" data-word="rejoinder">rejoinder</button> silenced the room; he explained that his new shielding would act as a <button class="word-btn" data-word="catalyst">catalyst</button> to neutralize the radiation. This was an <button class="word-btn" data-word="indubitable">indubitable</button> truth backed by rigorous physics. In truth, Kael was no arrogant <button class="word-btn" data-word="narcissist">narcissist</button>; he simply understood his ship's capabilities. With perfect <button class="word-btn" data-word="aplomb">aplomb</button>, he signed the final departure order.</p><p>The ship launched into the dark. Soon, they encountered a <button class="word-btn" data-word="virulent">virulent</button> energy storm that threatened to tear the hull apart. A <button class="word-btn" data-word="concurrent">concurrent</button> system failure disabled the main engines. Kael had to <button class="word-btn" data-word="extricate">extricate</button> the vessel from the gravity well of a collapsing star before the pull became absolute. He refused to <button class="word-btn" data-word="yield">yield</button> to panic. Instead, he devised an ingenious flight path. It was a clever <button class="word-btn" data-word="artifice">artifice</button> that used the star's own gravity to fling them forward. The maneuver worked, and a soft sigh of relief seemed to <button class="word-btn" data-word="waft">waft</button> through the cabin.</p><p>For weeks, the crew could only <button class="word-btn" data-word="loll">loll</button> about the ship, waiting as they crossed the quiet void. They began to feel an <button class="word-btn" data-word="unaccountable">unaccountable</button> dread of the unknown, a creeping <button class="word-btn" data-word="xenophobia">xenophobia</button> directed at any alien signals they detected. They feared that some <button class="word-btn" data-word="omnipotent">omnipotent</button> force ruled this empty sector. To ease their minds, Kael would display the <button class="word-btn" data-word="tactile">tactile</button> holographic maps, letting them feel the contours of distant stars. He sought to <button class="word-btn" data-word="kindle">kindle</button> their original curiosity.</p><p>Finally, they reached the coordinates. The scanners did not <button class="word-btn" data-word="gape">gape</button> at an empty sky; instead, they revealed a breathtaking nebula. The radiation had begun to <button class="word-btn" data-word="defoliate">defoliate</button> nearby dust rings, stripping them bare, but it revealed a glowing path. As the ship reached the <button class="word-btn" data-word="zenith">zenith</button> of its long orbit, the lost constellation came into full view. There was no need to <button class="word-btn" data-word="bolt">bolt</button> or flee; they had arrived. The ship erupted in pure <button class="word-btn" data-word="jubilation">jubilation</button>. The crew realized that the journey, like a true <button class="word-btn" data-word="sybarite">sybarite</button>’s feast of discovery, had given them a treasure that would last forever.</p>`
