    subtitle: "A submarine fighting a giant squid in steam-powered waters",
    content: `<p>In the steam-powered waters of the outer rim, the submarine *Leviathan* patrolled the deep channels. The vessel was a modern marvel, its steam engines pushing it through the waves. The crew was a diverse group of sailors, led by Captain Marcus. Marcus was a man of quiet, stern <button class="word-btn" data-word="demeanor">demeanor</button>, his focus entirely on safety. Today’s patrol was dangerous, as reports of a giant squid, a legendary beast of the deep, had reached the port. The crew’s chief engineer, an <button class="word-btn" data-word="assiduous">assiduous</button> researcher named Silas, worked to maintain the steam valves.</p><p>The ship was suddenly attacked. The giant squid, a monster of immense size, wrapped its tentacles around the steel hull. The impact caused a series of <button class="word-btn" data-word="seismic">seismic</button> shakes in the cabin. Silas had to control the steam grid, refusing to let the crisis <button class="word-btn" data-word="provoke">provoke</button> a panic. He was joined by a young sailor who was a bit of a <button class="word-btn" data-word="flighty">flighty</button> character, constantly complaining. Silas warned him to stay calm, refusing to <button class="word-btn" data-word="concede">concede</button> to fear. Silas worked to <button class="word-btn" data-word="retrieve">retrieve</button> a backup power supply, his movement precise. He had to <button class="word-btn" data-word="hew">hew</button> a path through a fallen pipe to reach the valves.</p><p>While they worked, a passenger named Donald, who was a known <button class="word-btn" data-word="misanthrope">misanthrope</button> and a loud <button class="word-btn" data-word="braggart">braggart</button>, began to shout. Donald accused the crew of being fools, claiming he could navigate better. He was a former <button class="word-btn" data-word="buccaneer">buccaneer</button> who had fled the law after a violent <button class="word-btn" data-word="incursion">incursion</button> in the south. He spoke like an <button class="word-btn" data-word="orator">orator</button>, his voice filling the room and using a local <button class="word-btn" data-word="idiom">idiom</button> to mock their efforts. He was full of <button class="word-btn" data-word="lurid">lurid</button> stories of piracy. Donald’s talk was a <button class="word-btn" data-word="derivative">derivative</button> display of self-pity, far from the brave herders of the sea. Silas ignored him, his focus on the valves. He knew Donald was an <button class="word-btn" data-word="apostate">apostate</button> to their code of duty, showing no loyalty.</p><p>The crew managed to launch a steam blast, which hit the squid’s eyes. The creature let go, its retreat a victory for the *Leviathan*. The crew celebrated their escape, their relief far from a simple, <button class="word-btn" data-word="opaque">opaque</button> silence. They had saved the ship, their success a proof of their <button class="word-btn" data-word="husbandry">husbandry</button> of resources. Captain Marcus promised to <button class="word-btn" data-word="promulgate">promulgate</button> a new safety code for deep waters, creating a formal <button class="word-btn" data-word="liaison">liaison</button> with the port guards. Silas sat by the boiler, holding a small copper gear, a <button class="word-btn" data-word="memento">memento</button> of the fight. He knew the danger was part of their trade, a challenge for those who had the courage to face the deep. He looked forward to a good meal, his interest in sea <button class="word-btn" data-word="gastronomy">gastronomy</button> strong, his <button class="word-btn" data-word="gregarious">gregarious</button> crew mates laughing. He knew their adventure was like a deep sea story, a tale of spirit and <button class="word-btn" data-word="temperament">temperament</button> that would inspire future sailors, far from the <button class="word-btn" data-word="esoteric">esoteric</button> talk of the court, their ship a safe <button class="word-btn" data-word="entrance">entrance</button> to the harbor, a victory over the squid’s <button class="word-btn" data-word="voracious">voracious</button> appetite, a success that was far from a simple <button class="word-btn" data-word="feint">feint</button> of the gods, their hearts filled with a quiet pride as they neared the docks, while a young passenger, who acted like a quiet <button class="word-btn" data-word="coquette">coquette</button> to the officers, smiled, and the crew was ready to rest.</p>`
